\f1\b\fs28 \cf2 III. System Processor (The Intentionality Loop)\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa200\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0\fs24 \cf2 The "Processor" is the logic layer that sits between the 
\f1\b Inputs
\f0\b0  and 
\f1\b Outputs
\f0\b0 , acting as a real-time state machine.\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa200\partightenfactor0
\ls1\ilvl0
\f1\b \cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	1	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Context Discovery:
\f0\b0  Asks "What world am I in?" by combining \cf5 \cb6 ActivityRecognition\cf2 \cb1  (physical state) with \cf5 \cb6 UsageEvents\cf2 \cb1  (digital state).\
\ls1\ilvl0
\f1\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	2	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
User Modeling:
\f0\b0  Asks "What is the user's intent?" by comparing current behavior to historical patterns and explicit intention settings.\
\ls1\ilvl0
\f1\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	3	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Output Modulation:
\f0\b0  Asks "What is the appropriate advocate response?" and maps the delta between intent and behavior to an intervention level.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa160\partightenfactor0

\f1\b\fs28 \cf2 IV. Implementation Constraints and Permissions\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa200\partightenfactor0
\ls2\ilvl0
\fs24 \cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Touch Pass-Through:
\f0\b0  Accessibility overlays are "Trusted Windows" and can maintain visual effects (dimming/blurring) without blocking the user's ability to scroll underlying apps.\
\ls2\ilvl0
\f1\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
The "Scare Screen":
\f0\b0  Privileged APIs like \cf5 \cb6 AccessibilityService\cf2 \cb1  and \cf5 \cb6 Usage Access\cf2 \cb1  trigger severe "danger" warnings to users. These cannot be bypassed and must be managed through transparent UX. \
\ls2\ilvl0
\f1\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Background Reliability:
\f0\b0  A \cf5 \cb6 ForegroundService\cf2 \cb1  with a persistent notification is required to maintain continuous sensor monitoring. \
\ls2\ilvl0
\f1\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Android 15+ Restrictions:
\f0\b0  New restrictions prevent apps with overlay permissions from starting foreground services from the background to combat "overlay-jacking." \
